{"task_id": "HumanEval/39", "solution": "def prime_fib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"\n    prime_fib returns n-th number that is a Fibonacci number and it's also prime.\n    >>> prime_fib(1)\n    2\n    >>> prime_fib(2)\n    3\n    >>> prime_fib(3)\n    5\n    >>> prime_fib(4)\n    13\n    >>> prime_fib(5)\n    89\n    \"\"\"\n    import math\n    from typing import Generator\n\n    def _is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if a number is prime. It returns True if the number is prime, False otherwise.\n        \"\"\"\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        for i in range(2, int(math.sqrt(num)) + 1):\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    def _fibonacci_generator() -> Generator[int, None, None]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Generates an infinite sequence of Fibonacci numbers. The sequence starts with 0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, ...\n        \"\"\"\n        a, b = 0, 1\n        while True:\n            yield a\n            a, b = b, a + b\n\n    if n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer (n >= 1).\")\n\n    prime_fib_count = 0\n    fib_gen = _fibonacci_generator()\n\n    # Skip initial 0, 1, 1 as these are not considered prime Fibonacci numbers for the sequence.\n    next(fib_gen) # yields 0\n    next(fib_gen) # yields 1\n    next(fib_gen) # yields 1\n\n    while True:\n        current_fib_num = next(fib_gen)\n        if _is_prime(current_fib_num):\n            prime_fib_count += 1\n            if prime_fib_count == n:\n                return current_fib_num"}
