{"task_id": "HumanEval/77", "solution": "def iscube(a):\n    '''\n    Checks if an integer a is a perfect cube.\n    '''\n    # Calculate the potential integer cube root magnitude.\n    # We use round() to account for potential floating-point inaccuracies when calculating a**(1/3).\n    root_magnitude = round(abs(a)**(1/3))\n    \n    # Determine the potential integer cube root, preserving the sign of 'a'.\n    # If 'a' is negative, its cube root must also be negative.\n    if a < 0:\n        potential_root = -root_magnitude\n    else:\n        potential_root = root_magnitude\n        \n    # Check if cubing this potential_root yields the original number 'a'.\n    return potential_root * potential_root * potential_root == a"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/78", "solution": "_PRIME_HEX_DECIMAL_VALUES = {2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13}\ndef _hex_char_to_decimal(char):\n    \"\"\"Converts a single uppercase hexadecimal character to its decimal integer value.\"\"\"\n    if '0' <= char <= '9':\n        return int(char)\n    else:  # 'A' through 'F'\n        return 10 + (ord(char) - ord('A'))\ndef _is_prime_hex_digit(decimal_value):\n    \"\"\"Determines if a given decimal integer value (0-15) is a prime hexadecimal digit.\"\"\"\n    return decimal_value in _PRIME_HEX_DECIMAL_VALUES\ndef hex_key(num):\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of hexadecimal digits that are primes (2, 3, 5, 7, B, D).\"\"\"\n    prime_count = 0\n    for char in num:\n        decimal_value = _hex_char_to_decimal(char)\n        if _is_prime_hex_digit(decimal_value):\n            prime_count += 1\n    return prime_count"}
